     "type": "output_text",
     "text": "## A0 context model\n\n**A0 \u2014 Control timed tank filling**\n\nThe function fills the tank for no longer than `TimerDuration`, terminates filling early on `LSHH`, and gives `stop` priority over all other commands. The initial and resting state is step 0, with both valves closed.\n\nThe model uses the required logical vocabulary. Physical I/O mapping and rising-edge recognition provide the interface between that vocabulary and the PLC tags.\n\n### ICOM table\n\n| Node | Function | Inputs | Controls | Outputs | Mechanisms |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **A0** | **Control timed tank filling** | `start`; `stop`; `LSHH` | `TimerDuration`; initial-step rule; filling termination rule; stop-priority rule; discharge inhibition rule | `fill_valve`; `discharge_valve` | OpenPLC Runtime; Factory I/O plant; Modbus TCP interface; command edge detector; sequence-state memory; filling-step timer |\n| **A1** | **Manage filling sequence** | `start`; `stop`; `LSHH`; `timer_done` | Initial-step rule; start acceptance rule; filling termination rule; stop-priority rule | Filling-step status | OpenPLC Runtime; sequence-state memory |\n| **A2** | **Measure filling interval** | Filling-step status | `TimerDuration`; timer activation rule; timer reset rule | `timer_done` | OpenPLC Runtime; filling-step timer |\n| **A3** | **Command tank valves** | Filling-step status | Valve assignment rule; discharge inhibition rule | `fill_valve`; `discharge_valve` | OpenPLC Runtime; output image; Modbus TCP interface; Factory I/O valve actuators |\n\nAll function names are verb phrases. Signal identifiers and the other arrow labels denote signals, states, parameters, or rules and therefore serve as noun phrases.\n\n## Child-function connections\n\nThe A0 decomposition has the following internal arrows:\n\n| Source | Arrow | Destination |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Filling-step status | A2 |\n| A1 | Filling-step status | A3 |\n| A2 | `timer_done` | A1 |\n\nThe A0 boundary inputs and controls are distributed to the child functions as shown in the ICOM table. A3 produces the A0 boundary outputs.\n\n## Control-arrow definitions\n\n| Control arrow | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Initial-step rule | Initialize the sequence in step 0. |\n| Start acceptance rule | Accept `start` only in step 0, with `stop = FALSE` and `LSHH = FALSE`. A start event during filling does not restart the timer. |\n| Filling termination rule | Leave the filling step and return to step 0 when `timer_done` or `LSHH` is TRUE. |\n| Stop-priority rule | Whenever `stop` is TRUE, select step 0 regardless of `start` or any other condition. Both outputs must be FALSE in that scan. |\n| Timer activation rule | Start timing on entry to the filling step and time only while that step is active. |\n| Timer reset rule | Reset the timer whenever the filling step is inactive, including initialization and termination by `stop` or `LSHH`. |\n| Valve assignment rule | Set `fill_valve` TRUE only while the filling step is active; otherwise set it FALSE. |\n| Discharge inhibition rule | Keep `discharge_valve` FALSE in every step. |\n\n**Filling-step status** identifies either **step 0** or the **filling step**. It is an internal state arrow, not an additional plant output.\n\n## Logical-to-physical interface\n\n| Logical signal | Physical tag / address | Interpretation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `start` | `StartCommand` \u2014 `%IX100.0` | One-scan event on the FALSE-to-TRUE transition of `StartCommand`; not its maintained level. |\n| `stop` | `StopCommand` \u2014 `%IX100.1` | Maintained stop condition. |\n| `LSH` | `LSH` \u2014 `%IX100.2` | Liquid detected at 2.4 m; available but unused by this task\u2019s control function. |\n| `LSHH` | `LSHH` \u2014 `%IX100.3` | Liquid detected at the 2.7 m overfill limit. |\n| `timer_done` | Internal timer status | Elapsed indication from A2 for the filling-step timer. |\n| `fill_valve` | `FillValve` \u2014 `%QX100.0` | TRUE opens the fill valve. |\n| `discharge_valve` | `DischargeValve` \u2014 `%QX100.1` | Always FALSE. |\n\n`LSH` is deliberately excluded from the functional ICOM arrows: the stated task does **not** stop filling at 2.4 m. Its mapping remains available, but assigning it a transition or valve-control role would change the requirements.\n\nThe child functions are a **functional decomposition, not a PLC execution order**. Their implementation must preserve same-scan stop and termination behavior without introducing a one-scan valve-closing delay.",
